      "proof_review": {
        "reviewed": true,
        "context_checked": true,
        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "Read the complete local chain behind Theorem3.15: inner-derivation support and finite fixed-scheme argument, twisted-trace orthogonal-complement construction3.3, semisimple symbol/fixed-Poisson scheme proof3.11, and full nilpotent degeneration3.14 including injectivity of T->T0 via the first nonzero coefficient and h-commutators. Finite Poisson homology for finite-leaf schemes, conical finite-leaf geometry and Jacobson-Morozov are identified established prior background. The theorem is selected once with every new support proof bundled, not as a one-line application of those results. The twisted bimodule requires an actual filtration-preserving automorphism of the chosen quantization, as in3.11; no unqualified lifting of every graded automorphism for every quantization is asserted."
      },
      "extra_source_paths": [
        "raw/sigma-2020-001-036/paper-014-source/sigma20-014.tex",
        "raw/sigma-2020-001-036/paper-014-source.zip"
      ],
      "statement_scope": "Theorem3.15 in its defined twisted-bimodule scope: X a normal conical symplectic singularity over C, A=O(X) graded with A0=C and Poisson bracket degree -2, reductive dilation-invariant Poisson automorphism group, and a Z/2-equivariant filtered quantization boldA. The chosen g is an actual filtration-preserving automorphism of boldA commuting with parity s, with graded image in that group. For its semisimple part g0, dim HH0(boldA,boldA g)^s <= dim HP0(X^g0)^s < infinity. Nondegenerate short star-products, if they exist, have the stated finite-dimensional trace parametrization up to normalization/scaling. No existence of such products, positivity, or arbitrary graded-automorphism lifting is added.",
